{
  "raw": {
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=2911": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry Job Department/School Chemistry FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Chemistry College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The Chemistry department at Adelphi University invites applications for adjunct faculty (part-time) positions. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,866 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . RESPONSIBILITIES: The successful candidate will be expected to teach general chemistry laboratory, or organic chemistry laboratory. QUALIFICATIONS: An advanced degree in any area of chemistry or a closely-related, chemistry-intensive field is required. A Ph.D. in any area of chemistry or a closely-related, chemistry-intensive field is preferred. APPLICATION: Applications must include a cover letter, a teaching philosophy, CV and transcript. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . For more information about the ACS-approved chemistry department, go to: http://chemistry.adelphi.edu . ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving almost 8,000 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers more than 60 undergraduate programs, more than 65 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and more than 35 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 116,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 64 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. College of Arts and Sciences: The College of Arts and Sciences at Adelphi University is a community of educators, learners, and citizens firmly committed to the principles of diversity, equity, and inclusion. We believe that these principles enrich our entire community, foster healthy discussions, improve decision-making, and enhance the educational environment and outcomes of our students. We support initiatives, activities, discussions, and practices that uphold the equitable treatment of all members of our community and strengthen their sense of belonging at Adelphi. We relentlessly strive to become a model for a socially just and inclusive institution. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3393": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Communication Theory Job Department/School College of Arts and Sciences FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Communication Theory College of Arts and Sciences JOB SUMMARY: The department of Communications at Adelphi University invites applications for an adjunct faculty (part-time) position to teach Communication Theory during the Fall 2026 semester . The course meets Monday, Wednesday, and Friday from 11:00am to 11:50am on Adelphi University's Garden City campus. RESPONSIBILITIES: The successful candidate will teach one section of Communication Theory, an undergraduate course introducing students to major theories, models, and perspectives in human and mediated communication. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering engaging instruction, assessing student learning, maintaining regular office hours as appropriate, and submitting grades in accordance with university deadlines. QUALIFICATIONS: A master's degree in Communications or a closely related field is required. College-level teaching experience is required. A Ph.D. in Communications or a closely related field is preferred. Professional experience in the communications or media industries is desirable. APPLICATION: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, current CV, and contact information for two professional references. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . For more information about the Department of Communications, visit https://communications.adelphi.edu/ SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,937 per credit. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi is one of just four companies and the only university on Long Island to be named among America’s Best Employers by State for 2023 by Forbes. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,400 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Brooklyn, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 70 undergraduate programs, 93 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 64 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 44 states and 76 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3327": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Nursing and Public Heallth Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: The College of Nursing and Public Health at Adelphi University is seeking adjunct professors for the fall 2026 and spring 2027 semesters (at both our Garden City, NY and Manhattan extension center locations). At the Adelphi University College of Nursing and Public Health, we educate the next generation of healthcare professionals to be committed to excellence as leaders in their disciplines. Our innovative evidence-based teaching and learning environments, combined with our collaborative healthcare and community partnerships, prepare students at all levels. Students will attain the necessary knowledge and interdisciplinary skills to excel as caring practitioners, health informaticists, scientists and scholars. RESPONSIBILITIES: Adjunct faculty will provide part-time instruction to students, hired on a per-course/per-semester basis and will adhere to all Adelphi Faculty policies and procedures, as defined in the Faculty Handbook. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Current Registered Nurse licensed in the State of New York is required. Master’s degree in Nursing is required. Minimum of five years of practice experience in specialty area (e.g. Adult Health, Pediatrics, OB etc.). Current BLS certification if teaching clinical. Current teaching experience; ability to teach across undergraduate and/or graduate curricula. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Strong interpersonal skills and ability to relate to students. Effective time management skills. Effective written communication skills. Project a professional and appropriate demeanor when interacting with colleagues and students. Provide useful feedback to students regarding their coursework and performance. APPLICATION: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter and a current CV with references directly on the Adelphi site to be considered. Direct any inquiries to Lena Garafalo (CNPH Adjunct Faculty Coordinator, lgarafalo@adelphi.edu ) and Sheryl Rosenberg ( smrosenberg@adelphi.edu ). SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,937 per credit. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi is one of just four companies and the only university on Long Island to be named among America’s Best Employers by State for 2023 by Forbes. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,400 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Brooklyn, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 70 undergraduate programs, 93 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 64 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 44 states and 76 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE COLLEGE OF NURSING AND PUBLIC HEALTH: At the Adelphi University College of Nursing and Public Health, we educate the next generation of healthcare professionals to be committed to excellence as leaders in their disciplines. Our innovative evidence-based teaching and learning environments, combined with our collaborative healthcare and community partnerships, prepare students at all levels. Students will attain the necessary knowledge and interdisciplinary skills to excel as caring practitioners, health informaticists, scientists and scholars. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3085": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Psych Mental Health NP Program Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty Psych Mental Health NP Program College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: As an adjunct faculty member in Adelphi University's esteemed PMHNP Masters of Science program, you will empower students to unlock their fullest potential. Join us on this rewarding path. The Adelphi PMHNP program is acclaimed for its commitment to rigor while supporting student success. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching specialty didactic and clinical courses. Assessing clinical competencies and theoretical knowledge while supporting comprehensive learning. Provide mentorship to the next generation of PMHNPs. REQUIREMENTS: Earned PMHNP master's degree or a post-graduate certificate. ANCC board certification as a PMHNP. A current, unrestricted NYS PMHNP license. Two or more years’ experience treating patients as a PMHNP. A background in education, whether through formal teaching roles or as a preceptor is preferred, but not required. Earned DNP, PhD, or other terminal degree is preferred, but not required. APPLICATION: Interested applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter outlining qualifications and teaching experience. A Curriculum Vitae (CV) detailing relevant academic and professional experience. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,866 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3315": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Psychology and Mental Health Counseling Job Department/School Derner School of Psychology FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty M.A. Psychology & Mental Health Counseling Derner School of Psychology JOB SUMMARY: The Derner School of Psychology is looking for adjunct instructors for Spring 2026 and Fall 2026 to teach evening graduate courses in counseling and psychology. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach a graduate-level course in-person with all responsibilities consistent with course planning and delivery. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum of a master's degree in counseling or clinical/counseling psychology is required. NYS licensed or licensed eligible. Doctoral degree is preferred. APPLICATION: Applicants should provide a curriculum vitae, degree verification and/or license, and the names and contact information for three references. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving almost 8,000 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers more than 60 undergraduate programs, more than 65 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and more than 35 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 116,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 64 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,866 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3363": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Adjunct Faculty - Theater Job Department/School Theater FT/PT/Temp Part time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Adjunct Faculty (multiple openings) Theatre College of Arts and Sciences Adjunct Instructor of Voice and Speech: The department seeks a dynamic voice and speech instructor to teach undergraduate performance courses in vocal production, speech, and text work for actors. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach assigned voice and speech courses. Develop syllabi and learning outcomes aligned with department goals. Support student growth in vocal health, expressive range, and text analysis. Participate in occasional departmental meetings and student showcases as needed. QUALIFICATIONS: Professional training and teaching experience in one or more of the following: Linklater Voice, Fitzmaurice Voicework, Miller Voice Method. Experience teaching undergraduate actors at varying skill levels. Ability to integrate vocal technique with performance practice and ensemble work. MFA or equivalent professional experience preferred. Adjunct Instructor of Movement for Actors: The department seeks a movement specialist to teach courses in physical actor training and embodied performance practices. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach movement courses for theater majors and/or musical theater students. Create engaging studio-based curricula emphasizing physical awareness and performance application. Collaborate with performance faculty when appropriate. Attend occasional departmental meetings and events. QUALIFICATIONS: Expertise in one or more of the following: Lecoq- based physical theater training, Clowning/Commedia, Viewpoints. Exposure in one or more of the following: Alexander Technique, Laban Movement Analysis, Suzuki. Demonstrated experience teaching movement to undergraduate performers. Ability to foster safe, inclusive, and exploratory studio environments. MFA or equivalent professional experience preferred. Adjunct Instructor – Acting for Non-Majors The department invites applications for an instructor to teach introductory acting courses designed for non-theater majors. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach introductory acting courses emphasizing creativity, confidence, collaboration, and communication. Foster an accessible and supportive classroom environment. Evaluate student participation and performance projects. Maintain regular communication with students and department leadership. QUALIFICATIONS: Experience teaching introductory acting at the college or conservatory level. Strong communication and classroom facilitation skills. Ability to engage students from diverse academic backgrounds. Experience with devised work, improvisation, or applied theater is a plus. MFA or equivalent professional experience preferred. APPLICATION: Applications must submit: Cover letter indicating position(s) of interest, Curriculum vitae or resume, Statement of teaching philosophy, Names and contact information for three references. Applicants must apply online at: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . Optional materials may include sample syllabi, student evaluations, or links to professional work. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until positions are filled. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving almost 8,000 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers more than 60 undergraduate programs, more than 65 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and more than 35 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 116,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 64 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary for this position is $1,937 per credit. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3375": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Accounting Job Department/School Willumstad School of Business FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Accounting Robert B. Willumstad School of Business JOB SUMMARY: The Robert B. Willumstad School of Business (WSB) at Adelphi University invites terminally qualified candidates to apply for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in accounting to begin no later than in Fall 2027. We are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to teaching students from diverse backgrounds. Adelphi is reviewing the recent governmental changes to the H1B process and is encouraging all qualified candidates to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching 18 credits per academic year (i.e., 3-3 teaching load) across undergraduate and graduate programs in accounting at the locations necessary to meet the needs of our accounting students. Candidates may receive up to 9 credits of research release (not to exceed 3 credits in any academic year) during the pre-tenure period to support their research activities. Teaching assignments may occur during the day, evening, night and/or on weekends and in a variety of formats such as face-to-face, blended, and online. The majority of our accounting courses are currently in the face-to-face format. Teaching interests should include ANY TWO out of the three undergraduate courses and ANY TWO out of the three graduate courses listed here: Undergraduate Intermediate Accounting, Undergraduate Advanced Accounting, Undergraduate Accounting Information Systems, Graduate Accounting Information Systems - Development and Evaluation, Graduate Financial Reporting Practice, Graduate Advanced Financial and Business Reporting. Maintaining an active research agenda related to any area of accounting. The business programs at the Robert B. Willumstad School of Business are AACSB-accredited and tenure-track faculty are expected to maintain Scholarly-Academic status by publishing in their area of expertise in refereed academic journals. Actively participating in WSB-wide and University-wide committees and contributing to Adelphi University’s mission and strategic plan. Providing academic advising to undergraduate accounting students every semester. Maintaining reasonable familiarity with the current technology in accounting including the use of AI tools and showing the willingness to build such capabilities in our students. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Accounting or in business with at least 18 graduate credits in accounting, from a U.S.-based AACSB International-accredited program. ABD candidates will be considered only if the degree is expected to be conferred by December 2026 for a Spring 2027 start, or by May 2027 for a Fall 2027 start. Completion of all parts of the CPA Exam prior to applying. DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience in using, and continued willingness to use current instructional technology and digital platforms relevant to business education. Potential and commitment to excellence in (a) teaching, (b) engaging in scholarly activity related to accounting on a sustained basis, and (c) working collaboratively with colleagues. APPLICATION: To be considered, applications must be submitted only through the Adelphi University website at https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . When applying, applicants should submit 1) curriculum vitae, 2) a half- to one-page statement of teaching philosophy, 3) a half- to one-page statement of research interests, and 4) contact information for at least three professional references. Do not send any professional reference letters until requested by the Accounting Faculty Search Committee. For any questions related to the search, please email Ganesh M. Pandit, Chair of the Accounting Search Committee, at pandit@adelphi.edu . Review of applications will begin soon after the applications come in and will continue until the position is filled. The faculty position is subject to financial factors to be determined by the Office of the Provost and to be approved by the Board of Trustees. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE ROBERT B. WILLUMSTAD SCHOOL OF BUSINESS The Robert B. Willumstad School of Business (WSB) not only prepares all our students, i.e., undergraduate and graduate, to become leaders who have a positive impact on our communities, society and the world but also supports an inclusive learning environment where all students feel understood, respected, and appreciated. WSB ensures that an environment of civility and respect is established to promote an inclusive, comfortable learning environment that facilitates the sharing of experiences and nurtures the critical examination of assumptions. To achieve this goal, WSB is committed to having a diverse pool of faculty. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $130,000 - $145,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3316": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Adult Health Nursing Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Adult Health Nursing (Two Positions) College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: The College of Nursing and Public Health at Adelphi University invites qualified candidates to apply for three full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Adult Health Nursing to begin in August 2026. Adelphi is reviewing the recent governmental changes to the H1B process and is encouraging all qualified candidates to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching across the undergraduate adult health courses – e.g., pharmacology, health assessment, fundamentals, and medical-surgical. A total of 18 credits/ year is required. Maintaining an active research agenda. Actively participate in the College of Nursing and Public Health and University committees and contribute to Adelphi University's mission and strategic plan. Student advisement. Assist with administrative activities based on candidate skills. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: A Master's degree in nursing. Research doctorate in nursing (PhD, DNS) or education (EdD) is required. Licensure as an Adult-Gerontology Primary Care Nurse Practitioner or Family Nurse Practitioner is strongly preferred, and national board certification in the area of specialty. A NYS RN license or eligible for licensure in New York State. Relevant clinical nursing experience preferred. Experience in simulation technology, online or blended learning, research, and education. Additional experience is preferred in other areas (statistics, research design, education, administration) as well as curriculum development and implementation across all levels. We are strongly committed to achieving excellence through cultural diversity and are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to teaching undergraduate students from diverse cultural backgrounds. Academic experiences with culturally diverse populations preferred. Interest in developing and implementing curricula related to culturally diverse populations. Experience with a variety of teaching methods. APPLICATION: Applicants should include 1) a letter of interest, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) teaching statement, and 4) contact information for three professional references. T o be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website only: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . Review of applications will begin November 14, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Upon further request, please send all professional references to Dr. Korede Yusuf, Chair, CNPH Search Committee at kadegoke@adelphi.edu. Faculty position is subject to financial factors to be determined by the Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected research and teaching university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 8,100 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students more than 50 undergraduate majors and 70 graduate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 115,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 41 states and 58 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE COLLEGE OF NURSING AND PUBLIC HEALTH: The College of Nursing and Public Health (CNPH) supports an inclusive learning environment where all students feel understood, respected, and appreciated. CNPH ensures that an environment of civility and respect is established to promote an inclusive, comfortable learning environment that facilitates the sharing of experiences and nurtures the critical examination of assumptions. To achieve this goal, the college is committed to have a diverse and inclusive faculty and thus especially invites applications from women, underrepresented, and historically disadvantaged groups. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $98,000 - $102,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3380": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Assistant Professor - Management Job Department/School Willumstad School of Business FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Management Robert B. Willumstad School of Business JOB SUMMARY: The Robert B. Willumstad School of Business invites applications for a tenure track faculty position in the department of management starting Fall 2027. Adelphi is reviewing the recent governmental changes to the H1B process and is encouraging all qualified candidates to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES: The successful applicant will teach three courses (9 credits) each semester at the graduate and undergraduate level at the School’s campus in Garden City on Long Island, New York, at the Manhattan Center in midtown New York City, and other off-campus locations. Teaching assignments in the School may occur during the day, evening, night and/or on weekends and in a variety of formats including on-line, blended, and face-to-face. The programs at the Robert B. Willumstad School of Business are AACSB-accredited and applicants must maintain Scholarly-Academic status by publishing in their area of expertise in refereed journals. Faculty members participate in course, curriculum, and program development, advise students and provide career guidance, and actively engage in department, school, and university service activities. QUALIFICATIONS: PhD or DBA in management/business administration or related field with specialization in Strategic Management with related field in digital transformation, technology and innovation, or AI related to management from an accredited university. The successful candidate should be able to teach a wide range of courses in management (e.g., Strategic Management, Business Policy and Strategy, Management of Technology, Team-Building, and Negotiation Skills). Candidates with ABD status who are on track to receive their degree by August 2027 may also apply. A demonstrated record of excellent teaching at the University level as shown by course evaluations and a record of or potential for scholarly publications are required. Ability to successfully teach and relate to a diverse, international student body is essential. Training and/or experience in data analytics/digital management is highly desirable as is professional experience in the business world including creating and managing one’s own business. APPLICATION: Applicants should send a cover letter, a current resume, evidence of high-quality teaching, and names and contacts of three referees to Jim Hazy hazy@adelphi.edu To ensure full consideration, applications should be submitted by November 2, 2026. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. For more information about the School, visit www.adelphi.edu/business . SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $128,000 - $132,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3401": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and MSW Program Director Job Department/School Social Work FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Associate Dean for Academic Affairs and MSW Program Director School of Social Work JOB SUMMARY: The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs provides oversight and leadership for the MSW and BSW programs in academic standards, explicit and implicit curriculum design and implementation, faculty development, academic affairs, and student achievement. This oversight extends to all program options (OMSW, Garden City, Poughkeepsie, Middletown, Hauppauge and NYC). The ADAA supervises the director of the BSW programs, the coordinator of the OMSW program, and the directors of Practicum Education and Student Affairs. The ADAA works in concert with the Center coordinators in the planning of center activities and focus areas. The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs consults with faculty around course assignments, hires and evaluates adjunct faculty, oversees and approves course schedules, and assigns faculty to courses within MSW program. The ADAA will explore areas for SSW growth and development, including flexible learning options, develop collaborations with state and community agencies, and identify and pursue federal training grants. This role also includes being the director of the MSW Program. While there is a strong relationship of the responsibilities of the MSW Program Director and Associate Dean for Academic Affairs specific responsibilities of the MSW Program Director position entail operationalizing key accreditation standards related to the MSW program’s curriculum processes and objectives, addressing student retention, academic progress, and degree completion. The MSW program director plans orientations for adjunct faculty, plans course scheduling, and monitors the implementation of the curriculum. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $140,000 - $170,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . REPORTS TO: Dean of the School of Social Work RESPONSIBILITIES & DUTIES: Ensures quality and integrity of the MSW, OMSW and BSW programs across all program locations: Provide leadership and supervision to the Director of Practicum Education, Director of Student Affairs, Coordinator of the OMSW Program, and Director of the BSW Program. Oversees the revision and updating of the BSW and MSW Student Handbook and Practicum Education Handbook to assure clear articulation of academic policies and educational processes, and consistency across school and university publications; Provide direction and leadership of academic administrators and administrative support staff responding to requests for exception to academic policies, preparing and tracking academic petitions for leaves of absence, withdrawals, late drops, etc. for BSW and MSW program; Provide oversight of assessment of students on leaves of absence to determine suitability for the return to the program; Work with Director of Practicum Education to address challenges in students’ progress toward foundation and advanced level competence; Facilitate communication and problem resolution in addressing academic-related concerns identified by students and/or their professors; Respond to student grievances in accordance with established school and university policies. Design, implement and maintain systems and procedures for working with students at academic risk: Oversee implementation of academic standards including development of academic probation contracts; Direct academic affairs administrators and administrative support staff in tracking and notification of students with low GPAs, students on probation or at-risk within the MSW program; Oversee processes around allegations of plagiarism and other forms of academic dishonesty and interpret policy and procedures, collect and file forms and evidence of plagiarism, refer egregious or repeat offenders to the Academic Standards Committee, consistent with School and University policies; Provide leadership to faculty, academic advisors, and the practicum education department around policies and procedures in the School of Social Work related to academic standards within the BSW and MSW programs; Develop and implement protocols to identify academically at-risk students to promote positive student outcomes. Curriculum design and implementation for the MSW program at all locations: Provide leadership in the delivery of a coherent and integrated explicit and implicit curriculum for class and practicum education; Consult with Curriculum Committee on curriculum implementation, curriculum renewal, and adjunct faculty development; Plan course offerings for all program sites within established time frames and in accordance with policy and procedures provided by the Office of the Provost and University Registrar; Consult with faculty around course assignments and assign faculty to classes, collaborating with Center Coordinators and other stakeholders as necessary; Provide guidance to the Chair of the Curriculum Committee to ensure that all curricula effectively operationalize the core competencies at the foundation and advanced levels and that all course syllabi are up to date and comport with established school, university, and accreditation standards; Provide leadership around licensing preparation and outcomes associated with the implicit and explicit curriculum and work with faculty to integrate licensing preparation within the curriculum. Student Advisement and Registration: Direct the academic affairs administrative team to prepare and disseminate program and advisement materials to support academic advisement processes that are responsive to the differential needs of the School’s diverse student body; Direct academic affairs administrators, center coordinators, and practicum education administrators to implement advisement and registration procedures; Liaison with University offices to assure integrity of registration processes and implementation of student academic affairs policies and processes; Direct academic affairs administrators and administrative support staff to ensure compliance with academic clearance processes for graduation from the MSW program. Student Affairs: Provide supervision and oversight to the Director of Student Affairs and Director of Practicum Education to promote the development of student activities and student engagement that is responsive to the differential needs of the School’s diverse student body at all program locations; Supervise and collaborate with administration and faculty to promote opportunities for student participation in formulating and modifying policies affecting academic and student affairs. Coordinate academic supports through external (University) resources for BSW and MSW students (e.g., Student Access, Counseling Services, writing and statistic tutors, career services). Committee Membership: Member of Dean’s Administrators’ Team Member of SSW Curriculum Committee (ex-officio) Member (ex-officio) of the Self-Study/Accreditation Committee related to implementation of the CSWE  Educational Policy and Accreditation Standards (EPAS) Member of the Practicum Education Committee Member (ex-officio) of the Assessment Committee Perform other duties as assigned. REQUIREMENTS: (Knowledge, Skills and Abilities) Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including experience in public speaking. Strong identification with the purposes and values of the social work profession and a demonstrated commitment to social justice. Experience in social work education, including demonstrated leadership skills through committee work and other activities. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work effectively with a diverse student body, faculty, administration, and staff. Ability to manage time in a fast-paced office environment, and to work on multiple projects simultaneously. Comprehensive knowledge of graduate social work education, current and emerging trends in social curriculum and social work practice. Strong management and organizational skills. Commitment to competence in using administrative and instructional technology. EDUCATIONAL/EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS: M.S.W. and doctorate in social work or an allied field is required. Minimum of 10 years post-master’s practice, teaching, and administrative experience is required. POSITION(S) SUPERVISED: Director of Student Affairs. Director of Practicum Education. Director of the BSW Program. Coordinator of the OMSW Program. Hourly Clerical Staff as assigned. HOW TO APPLY: To be considered, candidates must apply on the Adelphi website: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . When applying please upload the following documents: Curriculum Vitae. Letter of application (letter should include 1) academic leadership experience, 2) familiarity with master's and baccalaureate social work curriculum and accreditation standards, and 3) experience developing state and community collaborations). Names and contact information of three (3) references. (No actual letters. References will not be contacted without prior permission of the candidate). Three (3) representative publications. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected doctoral research university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 7,250 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students 79 undergraduate programs, more than 84 master’s degree and doctoral programs, and 63 certificate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 119,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 43 states and 72 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    },
    "https://phf.tbe.taleo.net/phf02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=ADELPHI&cws=43&rid=3318": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center New Search Login Page Position Description Clinical Assistant Professor - Graduate Studies in Nursing Job Department/School College of Nursing and Public Health FT/PT/Temp Full time Location Garden City, N.Y. Apply Now Clinical Assistant Professor Graduate Studies in Nursing College of Nursing and Public Health JOB SUMMARY: The College of Nursing and Public Health at Adelphi University invites qualified candidates to apply for the Clinical Assistant Professor position in the Graduate Program, to begin in August 2026. Adelphi is reviewing the recent governmental changes to the H1B process and is encouraging all qualified candidates to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching: 18 credits/year. Teaching responsibilities within the AGNP or FNP program (planned) primarily; however, all faculty may be required to teach across programs (BS, MS, DNP, PhD) Actively participate in College of Nursing and Public Health and University committees and contribute to Adelphi University’s mission and strategic plan. Student advisement. Assist with administrative activities based on candidate skills. Potential for FNP program director position. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: A master’s degree in nursing. Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) is required. Licensure and national board certification as a Family Nurse Practitioner required. A NYS RN license or eligible for licensure in New York State. Relevant clinical nursing experience preferred. Experience in simulation technology, online or blended learning, research, and education. We are strongly committed to achieving excellence through cultural diversity and are seeking candidates who have a strong commitment to teaching undergraduate students from diverse cultural backgrounds. Academic experiences with culturally diverse populations preferred. Interest in developing and implementing curricula related to culturally diverse populations. Experience with a variety of teaching methods. Experience in our other graduate offerings (statistics, research design, education, administration) as well as curriculum development and implementation across all areas. APPLICATION: Applicants should include 1) a letter of interest, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) teaching statement, and 4) contact information for three professional references. T o be considered, applications must be submitted through the Adelphi website only: https://www.adelphi.edu/hr/careers/ . Review of applications will begin November 14, 2025, and continue until the position is filled. Upon further request, please send all professional references to Dr. Korede Yusuf, Chair, CNPH Search Committee at kadegoke@adelphi.edu. Faculty position is subject to financial factors to be determined by the Board of Trustees. ABOUT ADELPHI: Adelphi University, New York, is a highly awarded, nationally ranked, powerfully connected research and teaching university dedicated to transforming students’ lives through small classes with world-class faculty, hands-on learning and innovative ways to support academic and career success. Adelphi offers exceptional liberal arts and sciences programs and professional training, with particular strength in our Core Four—Arts and Humanities, STEM and Social Sciences, the Business and Education Professions, and Health and Wellness. Recognized as a Best College by U.S. News & World Report, Adelphi is Long Island’s oldest private coeducational university, serving more than 8,100 students at its beautiful main campus in Garden City, at learning hubs in Manhattan, the Hudson Valley and Suffolk County, and online. The University offers students more than 50 undergraduate majors and 70 graduate programs in the liberal arts, the sciences and professional training. With powerful partnerships throughout the New York area, more than 115,000 graduates across the country, a growing enrollment of students from 41 states and 58 countries, and rising rankings from top publications and organizations, Adelphi is a dynamic community that plays a leadership role on Long Island and in the region. ABOUT THE COLLEGE OF NURSING AND PUBLIC HEALTH: The College of Nursing and Public Health (CNPH) supports an inclusive learning environment where all students feel understood, respected, and appreciated. CNPH ensures that an environment of civility and respect is established to promote an inclusive, comfortable learning environment that facilitates the sharing of experiences and nurtures the critical examination of assumptions. To achieve this goal, the college is committed to have a diverse and inclusive faculty and thus especially invites applications from women, underrepresented, and historically disadvantaged groups. SALARY INFORMATION: In compliance with New York’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $98,000 - $102,000. Adelphi University considers factors such as departmental budgets, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. An annual base salary higher than the range may be warranted in circumstances where a candidate has demonstrable equivalent prior higher education experience at another University. Adelphi University provides a comprehensive benefit package for faculty and staff employees. For a list of benefits provided to employees, please click here . Back Share Apply Now Adelphi University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We welcome applications from all candidates, including people of color and those who are, or identify as, members of any marginalized, underserved or underrepresented group. Adelphi is an emerging Hispanic serving institution so bilingual candidates are encouraged to apply. Here is our University statement on diversity: https://www.adelphi.edu/diversity-equity-inclusion/about/."
    }
